WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:15.287
Pollyanna Jimmy Bean straight into Aunt Polly's sitting room.

2
00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:18.169
"Oh, Aunt Polly!

3
00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:22.671
I have something even nicer than Fluffy and Buffy for you to bring up.

4
00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:24.472
A real live boy!"

5
00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:27.234
Pollyanna smiled broadly.

6
00:00:27.254 --> 00:00:32.197
"He won't mind sleeping in the attic at first, and he says he'll work.

7
00:00:33.297 --> 00:00:35.779
But I'll need him most of the time to play with me."

8
00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:44.403
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly's face turned white with shock and then red with anger.

9
00:00:44.423 --> 00:00:48.806
"Who is this dirty little boy?

10
00:00:49.226 --> 00:00:50.447
Where did you find him?"

11
00:00:53.408 --> 00:00:57.191
Jimmy hesitated and looked toward the door, but Pollyanna pressed on.

12
00:00:58.371 --> 00:01:01.462
"He is dirty, but I'm sure he'll improve with a bath.

13
00:01:01.822 --> 00:01:03.263
Just like Fluffy and Buffy did!

14
00:01:04.344 --> 00:01:06.786
He's an orphan, and his name is Jimmy Bean."

15
00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:10.810
"But what is he doing here?"

16
00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.594
"I just explained why he's here," Pollyanna said patiently.

17
00:01:15.614 --> 00:01:18.757
"Jimmy wants a home and a family.

18
00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:23.221
I told him how good you were to Buffy and Fluffy and me.

19
00:01:24.382 --> 00:01:25.944
And that you'd take him in too."

20
00:01:28.413 --> 00:01:31.475
Aunt Polly sat down and raised a shaking hand to her throat.

21
00:01:32.596 --> 00:01:35.578
The familiar helplessness was threatening to overcome her again.

22
00:01:36.839 --> 00:01:38.401
But she suddenly sat up straight.

23
00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:44.326
"Pollyanna, this is the most absurd thing you've done yet," Aunt Polly said.

24
00:01:44.346 --> 00:01:51.191
"As if mangy dogs and cats weren't bad enough, you bring home a ragged little beggar who—" Jimmy's

25
00:01:51.271 --> 00:01:53.673
eyes flashed with anger as he confronted Aunt Polly.

26
00:01:53.693 --> 00:01:56.876
"I'm not a beggar, and I don't want anything from you!"

27
00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.642
He stood right in front of her with his hands on his hips.

28
00:02:01.662 --> 00:02:07.024
"I'm willing to work, but I wouldn't have come to your old house if this girl hadn't made

29
00:02:07.064 --> 00:02:12.247
me. She said you were so good and kind—the nicest lady in the world.

30
00:02:13.468 --> 00:02:15.989
She also said you would be glad to have me live here."

31
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.252
As Pollyanna watched helplessly, Jimmy stormed from the room.

32
00:02:21.272 --> 00:02:30.692
"Oh, Aunt Polly, I thought you would be glad to have Jimmy—" Aunt Polly raised her hand to

33
00:02:30.792 --> 00:02:31.793
silence Pollyanna.

34
00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:37.114
She felt herself wavering as she remembered Jimmy calling her "good and kind."

35
00:02:38.615 --> 00:02:39.715
But then she rallied.

36
00:02:39.735 --> 00:02:45.077
"Pollyanna, please stop using that word glad.

37
00:02:46.437 --> 00:02:50.098
All I hear is glad, glad, glad until I can't take it anymore!"

38
00:02:51.658 --> 00:02:53.799
Pollyanna's jaw dropped in amazement.

39
00:02:53.819 --> 00:03:00.487
"Why, Aunt Polly, I'd think you'd be glad to have me feel gl—oh!"

40
00:03:01.628 --> 00:03:03.670
She broke off suddenly and ran from the room.

41
00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.414
Before Jimmy reached the end of the driveway, Pollyanna overtook him.

42
00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:11.556
"Wait! I'm so sorry!"

43
00:03:14.038 --> 00:03:16.420
Pollyanna was panting as she held out her hand to him.

44
00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.604
"Please don't blame Aunt Polly—she really is good and kind.

45
00:03:22.085 --> 00:03:25.728
It's my fault because I didn't do a good job of introducing you."

46
00:03:27.828 --> 00:03:28.989
"I'm not blaming you."

47
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.711
Jimmy shrugged and turned away.

48
00:03:31.731 --> 00:03:35.354
"I guess I can find my own place to live.

49
00:03:35.635 --> 00:03:36.755
But I'm no beggar!"

50
00:03:36.775 --> 00:03:41.479
"I do wish I could find someplace for you, though."

51
00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.663
Pollyanna was looking at Jimmy thoughtfully when she suddenly got a bright idea.

52
00:03:46.683 --> 00:03:48.765
"I know what I'll do!

53
00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:52.088
The Ladies' Aid meets this afternoon at Aunt Polly's church.

54
00:03:52.468 --> 00:03:53.829
I'll tell them all about you."

55
00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.652
Pollyanna was excited about her plan.

56
00:03:58.028 --> 00:04:01.912
"That's what Father always did whenever he wanted anything for his church."

57
00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:04.954
"Oh, no!"

58
00:04:06.075 --> 00:04:07.617
Jimmy backed away from Pollyanna.

59
00:04:07.637 --> 00:04:11.520
"It's bad enough having one lady call me a beggar.

60
00:04:12.761 --> 00:04:16.725
I'm not standing around and listening to a whole room full of ladies call me that."

61
00:04:16.745 --> 00:04:20.048
"But you wouldn't be there.

62
00:04:20.448 --> 00:04:24.032
I'd go by myself, and I'd tell your story better this time."

63
00:04:25.524 --> 00:04:28.326
Pollyanna kept talking as she sensed Jimmy changing his mind.

64
00:04:28.346 --> 00:04:32.889
"I'm sure someone there would be glad to give you a home."

65
00:04:32.909 --> 00:04:37.332
"I'm willing to work," Jimmy reminded her.

66
00:04:37.352 --> 00:04:39.814
"Don't forget to say that."

67
00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.216
"Of course not.

68
00:04:42.576 --> 00:04:44.637
Then tomorrow I'll tell you what happened.

69
00:04:45.758 --> 00:04:48.140
I'll meet you on the road where I found you this morning."

70
00:04:49.641 --> 00:04:53.844
Jimmy promised to be there and said he'd decided to return to the Orphans' Home for the night.

71
00:04:55.836 --> 00:04:58.717
"Even though I don't think they'd miss me," he added.

72
00:04:58.737 --> 00:05:02.238
"They aren't like a family, you know."

73
00:05:02.258 --> 00:05:07.299
"I do know," Pollyanna said sympathetically.

74
00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.661
Meanwhile Aunt Polly was watching the children from her sitting room window.

75
00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:20.283
She kept remembering Jimmy saying scornfully that she was so good and kind.

76
00:05:21.763 --> 00:05:25.044
And Aunt Polly felt sad, as if she'd lost something.
